  "workflow": [
    "User supplies lyrics; no new transcription text is inserted.",
    "Only an explicit alignment-button click starts the operation.",
    "Search each supplied phrase across the full recording and stereo channels before forced alignment.",
    "Resolve overlapping phrase variants and original ordering jointly.",
    "Verify weak passages locally; retain the original probability thresholds.",
    "Insert copies with stable IDs, preserve supplied originals, then align the expanded transcript.",
    "Repair abnormally long word spans only with compatible independent occurrence evidence.",
    "At a truncated recording ending, corroborate an existing complete supplied prefix with its observed next word across two audio views. Copy only that existing prefix; do not invent the unheard suffix. Uncorroborated candidates stay in review.",
    "Retain the contextual terminal boundary on a second click and preserve channel-disagreement review flags.",
    "After occurrence-span repair, retry every uncertain word with its neighbouring supplied words in mix/left/right local audio. Require probability >=0.5 in two distinct channel views, start/end agreement within 160ms, and non-overlapping neighbour bounds before averaging the boundaries and clearing review. Preserve confirmed manual words."
  ],
  "evaluation_scope": [
    "The holdout removes later exact-text occurrences from ten saved lyric records, resets all timings, and processes the complete saved vocal recordings with their matching instrumental stems.",
    "Correctness is checked against supplied text and earlier saved CTC timings, not independently human-annotated ground truth.",
    "Matching uses normalized text and start-time difference below 0.5 seconds. If an old saved word stretches over a music break, at least 80% of comparable word boundaries must agree instead. This rule is applied uniformly.",
    "The first and second production API results both pass word binding, finite in-range timing and preserved-row checks.",
    "This establishes recovery of all 153 saved-reference repeats plus one separately declared terminal-prefix regression under this protocol; it is not a universal zero-error or human-audited timing guarantee.",
    "Low-confidence flags remain. No automatic manual approval is performed.",
    "An independent Whisper probe on three short difficult excerpts returned unrelated subtitle phrases; it was inconclusive and was not treated as evidence of correctness.",
    "Original recordings and saved user lyrics are not overwritten by the test runner.",
    "Uncertainty flags are not cleared in bulk. Remaining weak or contradictory evidence stays in review; channel agreement is model-based evidence, not a guarantee of human timing accuracy."
  ],
